KG42.register("source_edge_archive-e15ce3f68f491b10c2f000b6",{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::E::v141-c-R010-E001","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R010","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-d90b7b5c0051250f","target":"COMP-9ca8822ee86e3e13","source_occurrence_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::V::clearing.local","target_occurrence_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","target_unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. | BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. | BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. | BMG stated time-slot pricing design. | General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. | General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e010","v141-b-g03-e016"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"860977c2755be39f4ecf80447d692199cec54b12a9a14a2001d7937c2db18506","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Submitted buy orders provide requested quantities and bid prices to local clearing, which allocates the highest bidder first and then lower bidders. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Submitted sell orders provide offered quantities and prices to the market mechanism responsible for local energy allocation. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Matching participants' buy and sell orders is specified as the means of achieving efficient local energy allocation. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price receive additional energy allocated through a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. Scope: BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers Condition: Consumers do not undercut the clearing price. Minimum and maximum energy-allocation constraints should exist, especially to account for prosumer generation constraints. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Different market time horizons should ideally be implemented, and allocation mechanisms must be tailored to achieve efficient allocation at each stage. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons Local energy allocation should preferably operate at near-real-time granularity. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Local clearing uses a closed order book and a time-discrete double auction in 15-minute slots. Scope: BMG specified double-auction mechanism","target_definition":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used. A clearing price is determined in every time slot; prices vary with demand, supply and socio-economic characteristics. Scope: BMG stated time-slot pricing design. Condition: When the described time-slot pricing design is used. Energy surplus should lower the microgrid energy price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: There is an energy surplus. A lack of local energy increases the market price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Local energy is lacking. The local energy price may exceed the external grid price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Socio-economic reasons, such as supporting local renewable energy, are considered. The electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Scope: BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. Condition: During this trial, in which the market mechanism was not actively used. Each transaction may have an individual transaction price. Scope: BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. Condition: If the proposed pay-as-you bid order book is used.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used.","expression":"p^{\\mathrm{clear}}_t = p^{\\mathrm{last}}_t \\quad \\text{(for the time slot } t\\text{; the resulting uniform clearing price applies to transactions in that slot)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_clear_t","x_last_bid_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g03-e009"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented. Hence, C4 and C5 are sufﬁciently addressed for operation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. | BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. | BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. | BMG stated time-slot pricing design. | General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. | General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e010","v141-b-g03-e016"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish general microgrid design, the BMG implemented virtual double auction, and the example EMTS; the original undercut statement is recorded as a source statement and is not rewritten on our own into the opposite condition."}});
